WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.596
Rear or centre?

00:00:03.876 --> 00:00:08.978
This small option decides whether one operator or two can use the same frame.

00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:10.558
In tight spaces,

00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:16.195
putting two separate stations back to back wastes floor area and doubles the frames you buy.

00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:21.224
They also block light and make it harder for a supervisor to see the whole area.

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:28.201
A rear-justified frame takes accessories on the front only, so it stands against a wall or a bench.

00:00:28.481 --> 00:00:34.599
A centre-justified frame takes shelves, pegboards, bin rails and power rails on both sides,

00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:38.229
so two operators can work back to back from one frame.

00:00:38.509 --> 00:00:42.294
That means one set of uprights serves two people instead of one.

00:00:42.894 --> 00:00:46.241
Furnisys Link Workstands and Link Trolleys come in

00:00:46.241 --> 00:00:49.589
both rear-justified and centre-justified versions.

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:54.743
On a centre-justified frame, load both sides evenly so it stays balanced.

00:00:55.343 --> 00:00:57.942
So look at where the frame will stand before you choose.

00:00:58.222 --> 00:01:01.133
Is yours against a wall or in the middle of the floor?

00:01:01.413 --> 00:01:05.727
Tell us below, and next, discover Flexi macro and micro slots.

00:01:06.327 --> 00:01:10.572
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

